Hi, welcome to Insure Nova Demo.

Insure Nova is Hexaware's AI LED framework designed specifically for modernizing legacy insurance applications.

In a typical insurance landscape, you can have decades old applications including policy admin system with millions of lines of code, complex business rules, tightly coupled components, and very limited documentation.

Before you can modernize, you would first need answer to fundamental questions like what does my system currently do?

What are the business capabilities embedded in it?

What can be sunset or retired?

What needs to be retained and what needs to be transformed?

Ultimately, what should my modern architecture be like?

Inshunova is here to give clarity on these.

It brings together AI agents, domain intelligence, and modernization frameworks along with your SME inputs as human in the loop.

To start with, legacy app understanding proceeds with defining a modern target state and results in a domain context in intact modernized application.

Let's look at how Rapidix has done it.

The capabilities section of Blueprinting helps you identify what your system is currently good at.

For example, this applications capabilities include streamlining, insurance operations, code processing, user authentication, code life cycle, etc.

Within each capability you will find sub capabilities and functionalities.

Within the sub capabilities you also have a process flow visualizer which will be able to tell you the process end to end using a flow chart.

For example, it starts with processing the e-mail queue, extracting the code, combining all the three codes, then storing and updating it.

Rapidix will also be able to intelligently identify certain insights.

For example, in this case there is a hard coded loop.

It's like it's telling that it's like a bus that stops only at 3 predetermined locations even if the passengers are waiting at twenty others stops.

These are important insights that comes handy and helpful while you are reimagining your system.

The other insight here is the system is checking the patterns sequentially instead of a single pattern match.

For example, it's going and checking with the person's name is John.

Then it's going and checking if it's Jane instead of directly looking up into a directory.

Moving on, every sub capability also has a detailed PDD.

This captures and organizes the existing business goals in a simple structured way.

It has detailed business workflow information.

It has flow chart.

It has the algorithmic comprehension.

This is like the process DNA of your system.

This can be downloaded.

This can also be edited as per your requirement.

The AS IS Business User story section gives you an understanding of the AS is functionality of how your business has been delivering value for multiple actors depending on the use case.

In in this case, the insurance underwriter is the user persona.

It gives the actors what they want, why they want it, and how it delivers value.

Every user story has the business value.

It also has the acceptance criteria and the boundary conditions.

We also have a blueprinting assistant who is like an SME chat bot with whom you can interact, ask questions, and then take informed decisions for target state blueprint.

SME can use blueprinting assistant to brain brainstorm solution options.

Like for example, let's say in this case I'm asking a question like there is a new mandate where every customer interaction quote and insurer handoff must be digitally traceable and auditable.

Now to execute this, what changes should I make to the current application?

Which flows get affected, which business roles get affected and how should the architecture look like?

The blueprinting assistant thought for a while and it is giving me a detailed analysis of the current system architecture, the changes required for digital traceability, what needs to be added.

Which business rules and flows are getting affected and it has also neatly proposed the target architecture along with an implementation road map.

This this is good, right?

This is where you get a lot of assistance, which is also domain rich.

It has the interior business knowledge of your existing application and then it is suggesting you how to proceed with the target state.

This platform is more than just visualization.

It's your knowledge companion giving SME's everything they need to analyze, optimize, and reimagine with confidence.

We move to the final steps, which is the modernizing part.

We call it the reinvent because this step isn't just about writing code, it is about using all the understanding we have until now to create a modern insurance platform.

The SMEs shall refer to artifacts generated in the earlier steps and can also use a blueprinting assistant to define the future state approach.

They can also perform additional analysis to generate custom outputs that helps support design decisions.

All of these outputs, the architecture, the PDD inputs, service definitions, and tech stack mandates then get fed into Rapidx Agentic pipeline where the expert would be guiding the AI to make decisions that suit the app modernization requirement.

Finally, we get the code in the to be or the target tech stack and the app will now be modernized.

To conclude, Insurnova is a structured AI intelligence driven journey from a legacy insurance environment to a modernized insurance application.

